Small modifies the attention mask and work schedule for isolated question branches,
adds bounded partial tiles, uses bf16 GEMM weights and Small's trained readout heads,
and implements a C++/Objective-C++ runtime. The optional TensorOps projection was
written against Apple's Metal Performance Primitives API and documentation.

The applicable Apache-2.0 license is in the Kai repository's LICENSE file.

The CPU lane-FMA organization, flop-sized task grouping and blocked attention were
informed by Hunch's eg2cpu (simd.rs and model.rs):
https://github.com/undrgrnd-labs/hunch
